pendencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!--\r\nIF YOU DON'T FILL OUT THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION WE MIGHT CLOSE YOUR ISSUE WITHOUT INVESTIGATING\r\n-->\r\n\r\n**I'm submitting a ...**  (check one with \"x\")\r\n```\r\n[x] bug report => search github for a similar issue or PR before submitting\r\n[ ] feature request\r\n[ ] support request => Please do not submit support request here, instead see https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#question\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Current behavior**\r\n\r\nCurrently when there are `global` and `window` global variables, the priority is given to `window` [with no additional checks](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/4.1.0/packages/core/src/util.ts#L15) in non-browser environment.\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\n\r\nConsidering that `window` has higher priority, it may have stricter checks.\r\n\r\n**Minimal reproduction of the problem with instructions**\r\n\r\nIn Node.js:\r\n\r\n```\r\nglobal.window = { foo: 'stubbed' };\r\nrequire('@angular/core').ɵglobal !== global\r\n```\r\n\r\n**What is the motivation / use case for changing the behavior?**\r\n\r\nWhen `global.window` is set on server side to provide fixes for client-side code in universal apps, this will result in setting wrong value for `ɵglobal` internal export. This affects [decorators, for instance](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/4.1.0/packages/core/src/util/decorators.ts#L13).\r\n\r\nThe same applies to other platforms (workers).\r\n\r\n**Please tell us about your environment:**\r\n<!-- Operating system, IDE, package manager, HTTP server, ... -->\r\nWindows 7 x64\r\nnode 7.2.0\r\nnpm 3.10.10\r\n\r\n* **Angular version:** 4.1.0\r\n<!-- Check whether this is still an issue in the most recent Angular version -->\r\n\r\n* **Language:** [all]\r\n\r\n* **Node (for AoT issues):** `node --version` =   7.2.0\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"mhevery","id":111951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTk1MQ==","avatar_